        "section": "sqlite3",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 697,
        "text": "Notice that \"?\" placeholders are used to bind \"data\" to the query. Always use placeholders instead of string formatting to bind Python values to SQL statements, to avoid SQL injection attacks (see How to use placeholders to bind values in SQL queries for more details).",
        "title": "sqlite3"
      },
      {
        "end": 240,
        "estimated_tokens": 73,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 4,
        "position": 0,
        "record_id": "801c3ac239e928d776230cf8",
        "score": 0.4368212158664222,
        "section": "sqlite3",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 0,
        "text": "* **parameters** (\"dict\" | *sequence*) -- Python values to bind to placeholders in *sql*. A \"dict\" if named placeholders are used. A *sequence* if unnamed placeholders are used. See How to use placeholders to bind values in SQL queries.",
        "title": "sqlite3"
      },
      {
        "end": 410,
        "estimated_tokens": 55,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 4,
        "position": 1,
        "record_id": "801c3ac239e928d776230cf8",
        "score": 0.4243212158664222,
        "section": "sqlite3",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 242,
        "text": "Raises: **ProgrammingError** -- When *sql* contains more than one SQL statement. When named placeholders are used and *parameters* is a sequence instead of a \"dict\".",
        "title": "sqlite3"
      },
      {
        "end": 1295,
        "estimated_tokens": 65,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 4,
        "position": 6,
        "record_id": "801c3ac239e928d776230cf8",
        "score": 0.41539264443785073,
        "section": "sqlite3",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 1088,
        "text": "Raises: **ProgrammingError** -- When *sql* contains more than one SQL statement or is not a DML statement, When named placeholders are used and the items in *parameters* are sequences instead of \"dict\"s.",
        "title": "sqlite3"
      },
      {
        "end": 797,
        "estimated_tokens": 48,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 4,
        "position": 3,
        "record_id": "801c3ac239e928d776230cf8",
        "score": 0.3580712158664222,
        "section": "sqlite3",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 658,
        "text": "Changed in version 3.14: \"ProgrammingError\" is emitted if named placeholders are used and *parameters* is a sequence instead of a \"dict\".",
        "title": "sqlite3"
      },
      {
        "end": 923,
        "estimated_tokens": 45,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 4,
        "position": 4,
        "record_id": "801c3ac239e928d776230cf8",
        "score": 0.35682121586642224,
        "section": "sqlite3",
        "source_id": "python-3.14.7-docs",
        "start": 799,
        "text": "For every item in *parameters*, repeatedly execute the parameterized DML (Data Manipulation Language) SQL statement *sql*.",
        "title": "sqlite3"
      }
